From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 13:29:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] msxml3: Use the node xmlAddChild() returns for text, which it
 joins to text before it.

xmlAddChild() merges text added after text into the text already there
and frees the node it was given; the DOM's conversion then wrote to the
freed node, which corrupted the heap.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/dlls/msxml3/node.c b/dlls/msxml3/node.c
index 706a5a07483..2606e99add1 100644
--- a/dlls/msxml3/node.c
+++ b/dlls/msxml3/node.c
@@ -5028,8 +5028,8 @@ static xmlNodePtr create_xmlnode_from_domnode(struct xmldoc_context *context, st
             xmlAddChild(context->tree, xmlnode);
             break;
         case NODE_TEXT:
-            xmlnode = xmlNewDocText(context->xmldoc, data);
-            xmlAddChild(context->tree, xmlnode);
+            /* text next to text, as from an entity reference, is joined to it and freed */
+            xmlnode = xmlAddChild(context->tree, xmlNewDocText(context->xmldoc, data));
             break;
         case NODE_PROCESSING_INSTRUCTION:
             xmlnode = xmlNewDocPI(context->xmldoc, name, data);
